A||||4||4Banger Bandit||Hey V6 guys!!! more ?'about my '87GT
Z||000000||4Banger Bandit||08-26-99||01:54 PM||||While taking my new car home, I noticed it shifted pretty funky... The RPM's would climb but the tranny didn't shift soon enough, and when it did, it chirped the tires.  When I got home, I noticed the tranny fluid was barely reading on the dipstick!  Now I'm guessing that was probably it but I'm not sure.  Could the shift cable be out of adjustment?  If so, how is it adjusted?  My old automatic camaro acted the exact same way when the engine timing was retarded too much, but what do these things Idle at??  Also, my oil pressure starts at about 75-80 lbs, and levels off at 65-70.  Is that about right???  thanks for all your help guys!
Z||000001||theogre||08-26-99||01:59 PM||||fill the tranny. check for leaks, try again.
Z||000002||Cliff Pennock||08-26-99||05:25 PM||||Yep, that's all there is to it. Just fill the tranny and everything should be fine.<p>You indeed need to check for leaks though. I would check the two hoses going under your car. In the middle on the driver side, these two hoses are connected to two pipes. This is the place where they always start to leak first.
Z||000003||4Banger Bandit||08-26-99||10:44 PM||||After adding 2 quarts of ATF, I noticed a SERIOUS leak!  I about shit my pants when I saw it.  But sure enough, the leak is pouring straight from those two hoses that run underneath the middle of the driver side to the tranny. I didn't feel like fixing it today, because I had just spend the ENTIRE day working on getting the engine tuned up and the body panels fixed.  hopefully I can tighten them, but maybe the hoses are cracked.  The car was sitting for about a half a year.  Has anybody replaced the hoses???  I hope I didn't screw up the tranny by driving it home with hardly any ATF.  Thanks again guys.
Z||000004||JetroGT||08-27-99||12:26 AM||||When I had my 86 GT I had a leak in the two metal lines running under the car. This was due to running over a wooden extension ladder while going up an on ramp at 55 mph at night.It didn't start leaking untill a month later. I just patched it, then sold it. I patched it by cutting out the bad section with a dremmel tool, then I flanged the two sides and clamped some rubber gas line to it. But if your going to keep the car for a long period of time I would get it fixed.
